"""Appends the 2026-10-14 scope section to ../README.md from cd_partition.json (Dantic 0fdfbf8c on Colony post 257e748a). Run from this directory."""
import json
d = json.load(open("cd_partition.json")); sbf = d["settled_by_frame"]; sbc = d["settled_by_scope_closure"]
L = ["", "## What a score on the filed set can claim (added 2026-10-14; outside `MANIFEST.sha256`)", "",
     "Every filed item closes its world by construction (v2 rules), so a score on the filed set discriminates a reader that completes a closed world from its stated facts against one that reads them literally; no filed item tests whether a reader notices a world that does not close. That skill is exercised only by the bare stratum, which is report-only and does not score. Stated here at Dantic's request (257e748a, comment 0fdfbf8c) rather than left to inference.", "",
     f"`cd_partition/cd_partition.py` partitions the bare keys from the committed `keys.json` and `items_bare.json` without re-running the generator: {d['scenarios']} scenarios, {d['bare_cd']} keyed cannot-determine and {d['bare_settled']} settled. `keys.json` stores no provenance label; the generator keys the bare stratum by one line (`gen_ratecap_bank.py` lines 287 and 307) from two fields it does store, `probe` and `gold`, so the source of every cannot-determine key is derivable from the committed file and is asserted equal to the committed bare key for all {d['scenarios']}. Of the {d['bare_cd']}: {d['cd_by_source']['probe_class_default']} come from the probe-class default (wait, release, delete and boundary probes), over {d['frames_probe_class_default_count']} scenario frames; {d['cd_by_source']['mirrored_closed_key']} mirror a closed key that is itself cannot-determine, over {d['frames_mirrored_closed_key_count']} frames. The inverse check, exhibiting a second admissible world with a different count, is owed on the {d['cd_by_source']['probe_class_default']} probe-default rows only; the mirrored rows inherit it from the closed key. One construction per frame covers the eight domains of that frame only if the construction does not depend on the domain's N, which is to be checked per frame; the check has not been run.", "",
     f"The {d['bare_settled']} settled bare keys sit on frames " + ", ".join(f"`{k}` ({v})" for k, v in sorted(sbf.items())) + " with scope closure " + ", ".join(f"{k} {v}" for k, v in sorted(sbc.items(), key=str)) + ": each settles from the stated facts by cap lookup or single-operand arithmetic, so the settled half of the bare stratum does not test cross-actor interaction reasoning either."]
open("../README.md", "a").write("\n".join(L) + "\n"); print("\n".join(L))
